WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.765 --> 00:00:09.794
This gallery collects scholar media for the course: the researchers and knowledge holders you are reading, speaking for themselves.

2
00:00:09.794 --> 00:00:16.776
Filter by week or by type. The tabs narrow the gallery to one week, or to videos or podcasts only.

3
00:00:16.776 --> 00:00:27.782
Read the card before you press play. Each card names the scholar, what to watch or listen for, and which reading to open next. Media is an on-ramp into a source, not a replacement for reading it.

4
00:00:27.782 --> 00:00:38.792
Load the player only when you are ready. Nothing contacts an external service until you press Load official player. YouTube then plays in privacy-enhanced mode inside the page; other items open on the official source site.

5
00:00:38.792 --> 00:00:48.809
Write your Reading Rescue note. After the media, write one sentence you can prove from the reading. That sentence keeps the media tied to evidence.

6
00:00:48.809 --> 00:00:59.755
Use the field prompt if your lens is on. With a program lens chosen, each card adds a prompt that turns the media into a concrete question about your future work.

7
00:00:59.755 --> 00:01:02.893
Watching is never tracked or graded.

8
00:01:02.893 --> 00:01:08.137
Where next: Open the reading the card points to in Readings and Media.
